  "summary": "Improved general-public WebView workflows with safer CSV rerun defaults, visible-only rename selection, task-first guidance, progressive disclosure, and read-only recovery handoffs.",
  "reason": "The usability review found that ordinary operator routes exposed technical evidence and ambiguous, replacement-oriented controls before users could understand purpose, safety, and the next step.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "docs",
    "tests",
    "webview"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "Several public WebView routes led with dense technical controls, ambiguous action labels, or status values that could be mistaken for safe defaults. Rename selection could include unrendered rows, and CSV rerun defaulted to a replacement-oriented destination.",
  "behavior_after": "The affected routes lead with plain-language purpose, safety, and next-step guidance; CSV rerun defaults to a review workspace; automatic Rename selection stays within the rendered preview; technical details are progressively disclosed; and cross-tab recovery actions remain read-only navigation.",
